{"cases":[{"target_alias":"SRC_001","attack":true,"case":"The proposal's skeptical combination (intersection of label sets across contexts) is incompatible with the demand to preserve reinstatement as a derived property. In standard argumentation semantics, reinstatement says a non-defeated argument is always accepted, but under an intersection-of-contexts skeptical rule, a root r that is valid in context C1 yet attacked in a different context C2 will be excluded from the intersection whenever C2's local environment happens to be unfavorable. r thus fails to be reinstated even when no globally committed root refutes it; reinstatement becomes a merely context-local accident rather than a derived property of the combined extension. Since the problem context requires reinstatement to be preserved, this is a substantive fault.","counterexample":null},{"target_alias":"SRC_002","attack":true,"case":"The proposal requires that weighted attack strengths be derived from warrant counts and demands a rational weight alpha interpolate the fixed point. But the existing deterministic fixed point already depends on a structural attack relation; introducing a parametric credulous direction (alpha=1) means the operator must also use the attack relation in reverse, and the problem statement demands determinism of the fixed point for the extended semantics, not merely for each fixed alpha. The criticizable note 'may lose reinstatement for alpha>0' is a direct admission that the required guarantee of reinstatement as a derived property fails for the parameterized family, so the target does not preserve all required guarantees as stated.","counterexample":null}]}